<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rŏtundĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis,f.
		rotundus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a round</i>
			
			<i>shape</i>, <i>roundness</i>, <i>rotundity</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemma rotunditatis absolutae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 11, 73, § 190</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. 18, 13, 34, § 130</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 23, 35, §
			86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">19, 5, 25,
				§ 76 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verborum,</span>”
				<i>a roundness</i>, <i>smoothness</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Symmachi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 1</span></i>
			.—Concr., <i>a circular space</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rotunditas dimidii cubiti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 3
					Reg. 7, 35</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
